"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project aims to revolutionize data analytics, with a specific focus on leveraging AI for data visualization tools (R&D proposals due July 20th). The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. By November, the project achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. The project has also reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule, involving a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing, with user interface enhancements planned for October. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the executive board approved a total budget of $2M for all phases, and the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000. A journalist from XY Newspaper, Kitamura, has requested an interview to uncover the full details of the project."
